Some more downsides:

Eating a panda should make the PC see things only in
black and white.

* Searching wouldn't work; something is either
   completely hidden or it isn't. This applies
   to traps as well as doors.

* Warning would warn only about the most dangerous
   monsters, there are no "middling dangerous"
   monsters.

* Enchantment is detectable, even with ID, and shown
   in inventory, only as -,none,+, no numeric values.

* Detect monsters would only show where they are,
   not what they are. Ditto detect treasure.

* Nurse dancing wouldn't work: an attack is an attack.

* Demons never offer to accept a bribe; enmity is
   enmity.

* Stuff seen is never seen by a color name; potions,
   dragons, gems, whatever.

More?

Another upside:

Grey-scale vision is more powerful than color vision
in the dark (thus the "eye of the tiger"), so the PC
should be able to see farther in the dark with the
same light source. This will _really_ help #jump-ing.

Overpowered?

